<p>This course lives entirely on this website — no separate LMS needed. Here's a quick tour of how everything works.</p>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#128204;</span> Finding Your Way Around</h2>

<p>The <strong>sidebar</strong> on the left shows every module in the course. Click a module name to expand it and see the pages inside. The page you're currently on is highlighted with a teal bar.</p>

<div class="callout callout--note">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128241;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>On a phone or tablet?</strong> Tap the menu icon (&#9776;) in the top-right corner to open the sidebar.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#128196;</span> Reading a Lesson</h2>

<p>Most lesson pages are organized with <strong>tabs</strong> at the top of the content. Each tab holds a different section of the lesson — click a tab to switch between them. Make sure you read through all the tabs before moving on.</p>

<div class="callout callout--concept">
  <span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128161;</span>
  <div class="callout__content">
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> You can use your keyboard's left and right arrow keys to move between tabs.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#9194;&#65039;</span> Moving Through the Course</h2>

<p>At the bottom of each page, you'll find <strong>Previous</strong> and <strong>Next</strong> buttons that take you through the course in order. You can also jump to any page using the sidebar.</p>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#128899;</span> Breadcrumbs</h2>

<p>The small links at the very top of each page (like <em>Home &rsaquo; PHIL 1301 &rsaquo; Unit 1</em>) show where you are in the course. Click any part of the trail to jump back to that level.</p>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#128229;</span></span> Downloading Handouts</h2>

<p>Some pages include downloadable PDFs — study guides, outlines, and other handouts. These appear as button-styled links. Click to download or open in a new tab.</p>

<h2><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#127760;</span> Browser Tips</h2>

<p>This site works in any modern browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge). No special plugins or software required. For the best experience, use a laptop or desktop — but everything works on mobile too.</p>
